<title>USA: Allstate Corp Q1 oper shr rises.</title>
<headline>Allstate Corp Q1 oper shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $1.26		    $0.76</p>
<p> Oper net		  559,000		  342,000</p>
<p> Revs		    6,179,000		5,903,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  442,000		  450,000</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call consensus estimate was $1.17 a share.</p>
<p>Net income was $767 million, or $1.73 a share vs $424 million, or $0.94 a share.  </p>
<p>Realized capital gains after tax in the first quarter were $208 million vs $76 million.</p>
<p>Personal lines written premium rose 6.2 percent to $4.55 billion.</p>
<p>The combined ratio, including catastrophes, fell to 95.3 percent from 103.3 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Statutory premiums in the life and annuity business fell 15.1 percent.</p>
</text>
